### create a room to read (run first, then replace :id below with the returned id) -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/new HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 2

{
	"name": "readable room",
	"visibility": "public"
}

### owner reads their own room -> 200
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/34 HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 2

### non-owner, non-member reads a private room they have no relation to -> 403 Forbidden
### findMeOneRoom now does an explicit CASL instance check via
### subject('Room', room) before returning, matching the pattern
### update()/remove() already used. Previously this was a 200: the
### @CheckAbilities(['read', 'Room']) guard only checked
### `ability.can('read', 'Room')` with no instance -- a class-level check
### ("can this user read *some* Room?"), not per-room -- so any authenticated
### user could read any room's full detail (messages, polls, members)
### regardless of ownership/membership/visibility. Room 24 above is public,
### so it still 200s for non-owners; a private room a user has no relation
### to now correctly 403s. NOTE: this same class-level-only CheckAbilities
### pattern is still present, unfixed, in polls.controller.ts and
### users.controller.ts.
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/18 HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 3

### non-owner reads a public room -> 200 (public visibility rule still applies)
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/24 HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 6

### room that doesn't exist -> 404 Not Found
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/999999 HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 2

### missing x-user-id header -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1

### x-user-id with no matching user in DB -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 999999

### non-integer room id -> 400 Bad Request (ParseIntPipe)
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/abc HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 2

### owner lists their own rooms -> 200, includes the room created above
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 2

### a different user lists their own rooms -> 200, does NOT include user 1's room
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 6

### missing x-user-id header -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms HTTP/1.1

### feed: user sees their own rooms + public rooms + rooms they're a member of -> 200
### NOTE: this route used to be unreachable because `@Get(':id')` was declared
### before `@Get('feed')` on the controller, so "feed" was parsed as an :id and
### always 400'd. Also, the public-room branch used deletedAt: 'null' (string)
### instead of deletedAt: null, which made Prisma throw a 500 on every hit
### once the route was reachable. Both are fixed in rooms.controller.ts /
### rooms.service.ts.
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/feed HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 2

### feed as a different user -> 200, includes public rooms + rooms they're a member of, not other users' private rooms
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/feed HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 6

### missing x-user-id header -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/feed HTTP/1.1

### x-user-id with no matching user in DB -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:3000/rooms/feed HTTP/1.1
x-user-id: 999999
